WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.180
[Bus engine and tyres. Music begins.]

00:00:05.180 --> 00:00:11.600
[Notification] Dispatch asks for Monday’s
on-time rate, and Tuesday’s if it is ready.

00:00:14.900 --> 00:00:20.500
Codex reads the departure log. Of the 18 buses
in the log, 16 left on time. Its answer is 89%.

00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:29.900
The operator asks ChatGPT to match
those 18 departures to the timetable.

00:00:31.300 --> 00:00:38.200
The timetable has 20 scheduled trips.
Two spaces have no departure in the log.

00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:44.150
The operator asks Claude to check
the dispatch records for those trips.

00:00:45.400 --> 00:00:51.800
Dispatch lists M17 and M19 as canceled.
Both were scheduled. Neither left on time.

00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:59.700
The operator saves a rule for future reports.
“Check every scheduled bus before reporting.”

00:01:00.100 --> 00:01:06.100
The rule and the dispatch evidence reach Codex.
It checks all 20 scheduled trips.

00:01:06.200 --> 00:01:11.800
Monday’s corrected rate is 80%.
Sixteen of 20 scheduled buses left on time.

00:01:15.900 --> 00:01:21.600
On Tuesday, a fresh session reads Monday’s rule.
Two trips still need dispatch records.

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:28.200
Codex drafts the reply. Monday is 80%.
Tuesday’s rate is pending. The operator approves.

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:35.100
Claude sends the approved reply to Dispatch.
[Mail confirmation]

00:01:35.400 --> 00:01:40.000
“Leave them your decision, the evidence
behind it, and a check they can run.”
